WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-I'm good.

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:04.304
-I'm so happy to have you here.
I do want to say something.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you're an Eagles fan.
-I am.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:09.409
-And so this, thus, ended a year
of being able to say

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:10.510 line:92%
you were the world champion.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just Philadelphia Eagles.
-Only last night.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.414
-Only last night.
But I hope you enjoyed your run.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.883 size:84% position:42%
It was a fantastic run.
-It was great, yeah.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
It happened in
my lifetime, so...

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so I just
want to say, you know,

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.623
I hope you got
the full amount of joy from it.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.759
-You're saying this like it's
never going to happen again.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:28.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I think now
it's just going to be

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
just the --
It's the Patriots forever now.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:39.472
-No. That's not -- that's not --
That's not nice.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Ah, yeah.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to -- Obviously, we
mentioned it tonight.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
You cover scandals
as they break, as well.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:48.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does this Ralph Northam moment
seem any different

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:51.084 size:81% position:41%
than what we've gotten
used to in politics?

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's crazy.
-Yeah.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.254 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Like, really crazy.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:58.258
Like, he's done everything wrong
every step of the way.

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:01.361
Forget the blackface thing,
which is obviously abhorrent,

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:04.330
and putting that on his yearbook
page and whatever happened,

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:08.802
but just -- This is like
crisis communications 101,

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:09.869 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
what not to do.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Like, he changed his story.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:18.111 size:84% position:42%
"It's me. It's not me."
He almost moonwalked.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:18.578 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-His wife also -- the
"Inappropriate circumstances."

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:26.019 line:92%
Like, obviously says that a lot,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, not just about
moonwalking.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I will give him
a little credit.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
He knows to look to her,
you know?

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:34.794 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You know what?

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've seen the clip so many
times, and, this time,

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really keyed in on her face
when he talked about,

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:42.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know, I won that
dance contest?"

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:46.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what?
What are you talking about?

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
You won --
Like, he's bragging.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.244
-At the end of the day, he wants
to get that detail out, as well.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:54.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Just by the way, I won."
Did I mention --

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:57.884
Like, you're all mad about
the blackface, but I won."

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Did you not
understand that --"

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.188
-It's like he's saying,
"There were a lot of guys

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:05.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
in blackface there who
didn't come close to winning."

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:05.792 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No. Seriously.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Imagine how embarrassed
they are."

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:10.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, by the way,
I was 15 in 1984,

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.332 line:92%
so I remember people dressing up

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
as Michael Jackson for, like,
Halloween or whatever.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
All you need is
the jacket and the glove.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:17.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's it.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:20.073
-Red jacket, white glove.
You're Michael Jackson.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:23.409
-Right. It's not like you had
to dress up like Ralph Northam.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody knows who
that would be in a costume.

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.212 line:92%
-That would be difficult.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:29.282
-So, there has been some --
Some of the Right have said

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:32.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
if this was
a Republican that did this,

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.286 line:92%
the media would be howling

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
at a much louder volume
than they are here.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:36.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Have we not been
howling loud enough?

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It seems like
pretty good howls.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We've all been in full howl.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:43.263
-I would like to point out, this
is the least we have mentioned

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:47.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
the president in
"A Closer Look" in months.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:47.901 line:92%
And I have to say, also, like,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were very conservative
in your estimation.

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
You said
"virtually every Democrat."

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.308 line:92%
I don't think there is a current

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:58.344 line:92%
Democratic elected officeholder

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:01.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
who has said
he should stay in office.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:01.781 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like not one.

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:04.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you can find a Democrat
to support anything.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:07.020 size:84% position:42%
You can find a Democrat
who supports Maduro --

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Republicans,
too, on the other side.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:11.257
But you can find a Democrat who
supports Maduro in Venezuela.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.793
You can find a Democrat who
says we should talk to Assad.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can find a Dem-- But
there's not one

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.463 line:92%
who is supporting him on this.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's really
unbelievable.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:21.868
-And what do you think their war
room is like right now?

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:22.702 line:92%
Because, obviously, you know,

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:25.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's made this decision
not to immediately resign.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:28.541
Do you think the conversation
is going to eventually lead him,

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:31.978
you know, when he talks to
his staff and his advisers,

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.379 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to walk away from this?

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I hadn't thought about
what his war room is like,

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.283
but that's an interesting --
That's an interesting question.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.385
-I mean, I'm assuming they move
the table against the wall

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
so he can, like --
when he moonwalks, yeah.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A lot of moonwalking.
-Yeah.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.725 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Red jacket, collar up.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's tough to know
when he leaves office,

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:48.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the issue
with the moonwalk is --

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:49.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
it looks like you're
coming when you're going.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It looks like
you're walking forwards

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:54.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're actually
going backwards.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.970 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know what kind of
war room it is,

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:03.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it doesn't seem like
there are a lot of generals.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.410 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, it's --

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't understand
the decisions being made.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.648 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a
State of the Union tomorrow,

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
a week later
than we were expecting.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:14.821 line:92%
We were talking backstage.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
You will obviously be
discussing it after the fact.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:20.893
Now that we're sort of into a
conventional State of the Union,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.295 line:92%
are we going to learn anything?

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:24.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are we going to
glean anything from tomorrow?

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.699
-I mean, I think no matter what
kind of speech President Trump

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:30.436
gives tomorrow, he's going to
continue to govern and tweet

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
the way he's been
governing and tweeting.

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:33.840
I mean, I think we've -- I think
the pivoting --

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is no more talk
of pivoting...or moonwalking.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.346 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, no, no.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:43.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He could give a very
unifying address tomorrow

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:46.886
and talk about the ways
the Democrats and Repub--

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
Somebody is
making better jokes up there.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:52.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
All the ways the Democrats
and Republicans

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:54.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
can work together and
this and that.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think everybody
is like, "Okay, we know --

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.499
Tomorrow morning, you know
what's going to happen."

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:00.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. And we were saying
backstage,

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the thing that I'm
looking forward to the most is

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:05.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Nancy Pelosi will be
sitting behind him,

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.773 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and he knows that.

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:09.208
And I just think, in his head --
-Yeah.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.176 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:13.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I predict a lot of him
looking back --

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anytime he gets a
standing ovation

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:19.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
from Republicans, looking back
at her and saying, like...

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:23.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, she does seem to have
gotten into his head.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, he doesn't
really know --

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
He hasn't come up with
a nickname.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He does seem to have
a grudging respect for her.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Democrats
stayed unified during

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:35.234
the longest shutdown in
American history, didn't budge.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:40.239
So I don't know that he's gonna
look, but he'll sense her.

